    "question": {
      ":question/id": "bad8a234-150d-5f78-89c4-27f02e958bc0",
      ":question/problem": "What is the coefficient matrix for the following system of linear equations?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}7{x}_{3} &=-6 \\\\ 5{x}_{1}-15{x}_{2} &=5{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we organize the system so that the variables are ordered ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}$ on the left-hand side, the constants are on the right-hand side, and every variable has a coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}+7{x}_{3} &=-6 \\\\ 5{x}_{1}-15{x}_{2}-5{x}_{3} &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 5 & -15 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
